  "title": "2026-09-08-reflow-152600 · sandboxed-tool-fleet",
  "description": "# Sandboxed tool-execution fleet\nRead the top flow left to right: agents submit an image and resource class, tenant quotas admit requests or hold them for fair retry, and placement claims a warm match or selects a healthy host and waits for cold boot. Ready environments receive fixed-term leases maintained by agent heartbeats.\n\nThe lifecycle at right ends in destruction, never recycling tenant state. Lease completion leads through idle and draining; missing renewals or maximum age trigger reclamation. Image retirement drains older instances without interrupting active leases. Maximum age also covers unleased supply.\n\nBelow placement, capacity, pool depth and demand drive pre-boot supply; repeatedly failing hosts are quarantined and excluded from placement. The lower execution region shows per-call time, memory and CPU limits, allowlisted proxy egress, capped output, explicit timeout results, and durable session-keyed artifacts. Operations tracks boot latency, reclamations, timeouts and escape-attempt signals.",
  "mode": "diagram",
